      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="1012.0778v2-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Background: Many biological systems are modeled qualitatively with discrete models, such as probabilistic Boolean networks, logical models, Petri nets, and agent-based models, with the goal to gain a better understanding of the system. The computational complexity to analyze the complete dynamics of these models grows exponentially in the number of variables, which impedes working with complex mod&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('1012.0778v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('1012.0778v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
